FP6 mir-upgrade (Mir 2.28); the source changes are version-guarded:
 * miroil::SurfaceObserver::mirror_mode_set_to (new pure virtual): no-op.
 * tests/framework/fake_mirsurface.h (FP6 native lifecycle test): no
   override on the frame-dropper/buffer-count methods Mir >= 2.20 dropped.
 * The privacy-lock restriction also covers the privileged globals Mir 2.28
   adds (ext-foreign-toplevel-list, ext-image-copy-capture,
   ext-output-image-capture-source, ext-session-lock): offered to nobody
   unless FP6_WAYLAND_PRIVILEGED_ALLOW_ALL=1.
 * Mir's own session lock (Mir 2.28 follows logind Lock/Unlock) is logged.
Applied after qtmir-mir2-28-upstream.patch.
